completed_at: "2026-08-09T13:50:01.280Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A declaration records what happens when its owner reaches a terminal status, and the default is continued enforcement rather than silence; Explicit retirement requires a recorded reason naming why the guarded property stopped mattering, and a retirement without one fails the gate; A canceled owner never retires a bound implicitly, because abandoning remediation is not evidence that the hazard is gone; A held declaration keeps reporting its observed value and drift, so no number in the document is both stale and indistinguishable from a current one; dependency-kind-blocks and dependency-kind-related-to are re-declared at their true current counts and held, so both populations are guarded against regrowth; A negative control proves that a held bound fails when its population grows after the owner closed"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Bound lifetime declared independently of owner lifecycle, defaulting to continued enforcement"
expected_result: "A declaration keeps enforcing after its owning item reaches a terminal status unless it explicitly declares retirement with a recorded reason, and the two populations that drifted while unguarded are held at their true counts."
actual_result: "Shipped. on_owner_terminal defaults to hold; retire requires a non-empty retired_reason and fails as retirement_reason_missing without one; an out-of-domain disposition fails rather than defaulting. dependency-kind-blocks re-declared 241 to 243 and dependency-kind-related-to 43 to 50, both held. Gate reports 26 enforced, 3 held, 0 retired against 23 enforced and 3 retired before. Negative control extended to four declarations, including one proving a held bound still fails after its owner closed."
