comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T13:36:51.575Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence, measured and then shipped in one pass at commit 9a0a048b6.\n\nMeasurement before the change. The gate reported twenty-three enforced and three retired declarations. All twenty-three enforced declarations sat at observed equal to bound exactly. The only declarations whose observed value had drifted from what they declared were the retired ones: dependency-kind-blocks declared 241 and observed 243, dependency-kind-related-to declared 43 and observed 50, both reporting ok true with reason retired_with_owner. The third retired declaration, graph-finding-legacy-ordering-cycle, observed 49 against a declared 49 and had not drifted.\n\nTimeline reconstructed from dependency row created_at values. The rows that carried both populations past their ceilings were written on 2026-08-08 between 21:55Z and 22:50Z by ordinary maintenance sessions through the supported surface. Both owning items reached closed at roughly 23:25Z the same evening. The breach therefore existed for about ninety minutes while the bounds were still enforced, and was never reported, because the next evaluation ran after retirement.\n\nBoth fixes verified genuine, in a sandbox tracker at this commit, so that neither retirement is mistaken for a bad decision. Writing a dependency of kind related_to now stores kind related, confirming that pm-4020c5's canonical write contract shipped and that this population can no longer grow. A reverse blocks row now classifies its dependent as blocked under pm next, confirming that pm-jkbqt8's corpus-aware reverse resolution shipped and that blocks rows are no longer invisible to readiness. The decisions were right; the vocabulary had no state in which to record them, so the only available outcome was silence.\n\nContrast that motivated the fix. The surface replication gate in the same directory honours a waiver only while it names a pm item and carries an expires_on that is greater than or equal to today, so a suppression there decays and enforcement resumes. The measurement ratchet had the inverse lifetime: the bound decayed and enforcement ended permanently. Two gates, one directory, opposite polarities, nothing reconciling them.\n\nChange shipped. Declarations now carry an on_owner_terminal disposition. The default is hold, so a bound keeps comparing after its owner closes or is canceled. Setting it to retire stops the comparison and requires a non-empty retired_reason, so dropping a guard is a recorded decision; a retirement without a reason fails with retirement_reason_missing. A disposition outside the domain fails with owner_terminal_disposition_not_declared rather than falling back to the default, because silently defaulting an unreadable disposition is how a guard disappears without anyone deciding it should. The re-baseline path still skips explicitly retired declarations and now re-baselines held ones like any other, tighten-only in both polarities. The failure text no longer advises moving the owning item to a terminal status, which was the exact escape hatch this item was filed about.\n\nBoth drifted bounds re-declared at their true current counts, 243 and 50, measured on 2026-08-09, each with a note recording that its fix shipped, that the sandbox probe confirmed it, and why the population is now held rather than retired. related_to is held rather than retired even though it can no longer grow, because holding a frozen population costs nothing and is precisely what would catch a regression in the write-time canonicalization.\n\nResult. The gate now reports twenty-six enforced, three of them held past a finished owner, and zero retired, against twenty-three enforced and three retired before. Two populations that were unguarded are guarded again at their true values.\n\nNegative control extended from two declarations to four, and passes. The two lifetime controls are the ones that could not have passed before: negative-control-held-past-closed-owner declares a ceiling of zero owned by a closed item and reports ceiling_exceeded, proving a terminal owner no longer stops the comparison, and negative-control-retirement-without-reason reports retirement_reason_missing. The held control is identified by declaration id rather than by reason, because it shares ceiling_exceeded with the plain ceiling control and the property it proves is that the comparison ran at all.\n\nIncidental correction to a standing note. pm create does accept --close-reason. The negative control's seeded closed owner was refused with close_reason_required under governance.require_close_reason, and the refusal envelope named the flag in its own examples, which is a small piece of evidence that closed value domains that teach their own recovery are reachable today.\n"
  "2026-08-09T14:18:53.189Z","harness:claude-code","CI escape on the first push, fixed in the follow-up. Two jobs failed at commit f6deae17c. Gates (static) reported evaluateDeclaration at complexity 17 against a cap of 16, because the added disposition fields each carry optional chaining and optional chaining counts toward the cap; the invariant half of the observation is now built by resolveObservationBase, which is the same remedy the ratchet's earlier polarity work used when nested ternaries hit 24. Gates (coverage) reported 99.99 percent, from the one branch the new negative control cannot reach on a passing run: the failure path asserting that the held bound was proved against a closed owner specifically. A fiftieth test now drives it by seeding the terminal owner as canceled, so both lifetime reasons still fire while the closed-owner assertion does not, which is the only state that isolates that branch. Local verification afterwards: eslint clean, full lint clean, coverage exactly 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts, tracker ratchet 26 enforced with 3 held and 0 retired, negative control passing all four declarations. Worth recording that pnpm quality:static passed locally throughout and never runs eslint, so the complexity cap is reachable only through pnpm lint or hosted CI - a local and hosted gap of the same shape as pm-xgah3a, and the reason the escape was not caught before pushing."
